  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Mikhail bangs on the locked office door calling Victor a traitor, but Chef Barinov assigns Senya to guard the door while he goes to the market. Meanwhile, Vika insists on her contracted hospital.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ты зачем меня тут закрыл?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Чтобы ты глупостей не наделал!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Витя, ты настоящий предатель!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сеня, я поехал на рынок.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты охраняешь покой Михаила Джековича.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Если он выйдет, башку оторву.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "А если не выйдет, премию дадите?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Пять тысяч пинков под зад.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Спасибо, отличный у меня аванс.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Тихо, не кричи, я нашёл дорогу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Тут поблизости есть другой роддом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ладно, поедем по контракту.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ты зачем меня тут закрыл?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why did you lock me in here?' The grammar packs 'you' and 'to close' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Чтобы ты глупостей не наделал!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'So that you do not do anything foolish!' In Russian, the idea of 'so that' flows naturally into 'make' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Витя, ты настоящий предатель!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Vitya, you are a real traitor!' Notice how Russian expresses 'proper name' and 'traitor' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сеня, я поехал на рынок.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Senya, I am heading to the market.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'Senya' before landing on 'market'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты охраняешь покой Михаила Джековича.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are guarding Mikhail Dzhekovich's peace.' The meaning hinges on 'you' working together with 'proper name' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Если он выйдет, башку оторву.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'If he comes out, I will tear your head off.' In Russian, the idea of 'if' flows naturally into 'to tear off' without extra filler words. Senya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "А если не выйдет, премию дадите?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And if he does not come out, will you give me a bonus?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'and' before landing on 'will give'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Пять тысяч пинков под зад.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Five thousand kicks in the backside.' Notice how Russian expresses 'five' and 'backside' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Спасибо, отличный у меня аванс.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Thanks, that is a great advance for me.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'thank you' and finishing on 'advance'. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Тихо, не кричи, я нашёл дорогу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Quiet, do not shout, I found the way.' Notice how Russian expresses 'quiet' and 'road' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Тут поблизости есть другой роддом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'There is another maternity hospital nearby.' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'here', while 'maternity hospital' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ладно, поедем по контракту.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Alright, we will go under the contract.' The grammar packs 'all right' and 'contract' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
